  "task": "X80 odd-support free scaling orbits",
  "theorem": "If n is a power of two and A is an odd-cardinality subset of mu_n, then the multiplicative stabilizer of A inside mu_n is trivial.  Hence ordered h=5 pairs have free scaling orbits.  Each free ordered-pair orbit has n members and exactly h anchored representatives with 1 in the first support, so full ordered row count equals (n/h) times anchored count.  For unordered h=5 pairs, the only possible nontrivial stabilizer is the antipodal swap P <-> -P."
